                <pb facs="0568" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.51/227: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cottrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-28T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 28,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Your 48, December 21, 9 a.m.</p>
                <p>Department not impressed with the views of the President given in your
                    telegram.</p>
                <p>You are requested to present in a formal note the views and protests of the
                    Equitable Trust Company as set forth in the Department’s telegram No. 25,
                    December 19, 6 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
